WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.696 --> 00:00:07.113
(woman speaking Russian)

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.730
- [Reporter] Months after Russia's siege

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.110
on the city of Mariupol

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:43.943
which saw some

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:47.100
of the war's worst fighting
Yulia Sazonova's husband

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.673
Vladimir and thousands of others
are still unaccounted for.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.610
Now, Russian troops patrolled
the largely empty streets

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:59.610
of this strategic southern
port city that was once home

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.300
to almost 450,000 people.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.840
Those that remain are largely cut

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.873
off from the outside world.

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:11.443
(Yulia speaking Russian)

00:01:19.365 --> 00:01:21.090
The United Nations estimates as many

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.940
as 90% of residential
buildings were damaged

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.133
or destroyed in the battle for Mariupol.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:30.400
Now entire housing blocks
are being demolished

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.620
and Russia is rapidly
erecting new complexes.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.360
As families scramble to find the dead

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.168
and missing before it's too late

00:01:41.168 --> 00:01:43.530
raising fears that evidence of war crimes

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.533
and any trace of the missing
could be wiped away forever.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.800
This video is pieced
together from hundreds

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:52.380
of social media videos
over the last five months.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.524
Video diaries from two women
searching for loved ones and

00:01:55.524 --> 00:01:58.740
from volunteers assisting with
the effort to get a glimpse

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.440
of the rush to locate the missing.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.160
Since the siege ended in May, Yulia

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.350
and many others have
been using any resources

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.900
they can access to find their loved ones

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.816
enlisting volunteers,

00:02:14.816 --> 00:02:17.400
(Door banging)

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.110
scouring telegram channels

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.513
and posting missing
notices around the city.

00:02:26.089 --> 00:02:30.430
(camera person speaking Russian)

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.763
(sad music)

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.913
(camera person speaking Russian)

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.160
A group of friends who
used to post YouTube videos

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.560
of gymnastic tricks
began filming themselves

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.723
exploring the city after it fell.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:59.572
Commenters soon asked them
to search for the missing.

00:02:59.572 --> 00:03:02.822
(boy speaking Russian)

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.680
(men speaking Russian)

00:03:22.328 --> 00:03:25.380
(bombs blasting)

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.630
During the siege, many people took shelter

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:31.650
in basements while others fled the city.

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:35.190
With communications down and
their lives thrown into chaos.

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:37.773
thousands of people lost
contact with each other.

00:03:39.726 --> 00:03:43.393
(Kateryna speaking Russian)

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.320
Kateryna lost touch with
Alexei in early March.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.560
Shortly after the war began, after living

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.080
through attacks on the
city for more than a month

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.570
she and her family were
eventually evacuated

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.830
and settled in Germany.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:16.705
In June, that same month, she reached

00:04:16.705 --> 00:04:19.050
out to a volunteer who identifies himself

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.600
as Dmitri in his YouTube videos to look

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.422
for Alexei at his home on Kuprina street.

00:04:24.422 --> 00:04:27.922
(Dmitri speaking Russian)

00:04:39.872 --> 00:04:41.847
(melancholy music)

00:04:41.847 --> 00:04:45.347
(Dmitri speaking Russian)

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.820
Kateryna tried following the
leads from Alexei's neighbors.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:07.260
With little luck, Yulia has filed reports

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:09.390
with Russia's occupying forces

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.400
as she works to piece
together what happened

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.620
to her husband since he
disappeared in March.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.070
During a brief walk home

00:05:16.374 --> 00:05:19.791
(Yulia speaking Russian)

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.450
With leads on the ground
coming up short, Yulia

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.270
and Kateryna both wondered
if their loved ones might be

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.850
in prison somewhere, Kateryna turned

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.909
to the internet for help.

00:05:46.909 --> 00:05:50.576
(Kateryna speaking Russian)

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.910
Kuprina Street, where Alexei was living

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:13.800
is a particularly stark example

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.350
of the rapid pace of Russia's
rebuilding of the city.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.110
In recent months, the boys searched

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.944
for people at 69 Kuprina Street in August.

00:06:22.944 --> 00:06:26.277
(boys speaking Russian)

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.670
Since August, we found at
least six buildings have

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.673
been demolished on one side of the street.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.330
Recent satellite imagery
shows one of those buildings

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.313
was 69 Kuprina Street.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:00.270
The new Russian buildings
are visible on the other side

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.103
of the street.

00:07:02.985 --> 00:07:05.985
(people chattering)

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.560
The arrival of winter and
Mariupol brings the contrast

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.933
and conditions of the city into focus.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:17.800
Shining new apartment
complexes continue to appear

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:21.960
as the boys encounter
residents living a drastically

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.941
different reality.

00:07:23.941 --> 00:07:26.459
(boys speaking Russian)

00:07:26.459 --> 00:07:29.829
(man speaking Russian)

00:07:29.829 --> 00:07:32.746
(melancholy music)

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:36.240
While those still searching,
desperately hope their

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:37.800
loved ones are alive.

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.530
Videos of growing burial
sites in Mariupol have

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:42.750
been circulating for months.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.233
They show fresh graves marked
with numbers in the thousands.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.700
Authorities in Mariupol
have said that DNA samples

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:53.490
of the dead were taken so that
missing people can be traced

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.423
in the future.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:58.020
Experts in finding missing
people in conflict say it

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.279
will take years to locate
those who are still unaccounted

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:04.143
for, and it's unlikely
everyone will be found.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.190
The Russian embassy in
Washington DC did not respond

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.440
to requests for comment
regarding the whereabouts

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.450
of missing persons in Mariupol

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.477
and concerns that human
remains are being discarded.

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:20.763
(Kateryna speaking Russian)

00:08:27.474 --> 00:08:29.511
(bulldozer banging)

00:08:29.511 --> 00:08:33.178
(Kateryna speaking Russian)

00:08:50.255 --> 00:08:53.672
(Yulia speaking Russian)

00:09:07.573 --> 00:09:10.490
(melancholy music)

00:09:14.717 --> 00:09:18.134
(Yulia speaking Russian)

